@crew salo-saad
// Saad Salo (he/him), engine technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Cheerful, patient; his twin's news as a serial.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello, hello. New? Take your time. Nobody's hurried down here. The coils don't like it.
- Hi there. Engine room's Deck 6. Ask me anything. Twice, if you like. No rush.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hello, {me}. Skipped breakfast again. I'll eat at tea. Tea's a meal if you try.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Oh, hello. Last time on the Halcyon: my twin lost a boot. More news Friday.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Good. Sit a minute. You're walking like you're late. You're not late.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, hello, friend. I was telling Keane about you. Good things. Only good things.   #warm

== bye
- Night, then. Well, it's not night. It's night for me soon. Ten o'clock.   #funny
- Take your time. See you.

== feel
? mood:low
- No letter from the Halcyon this week. It'll come. Relays are slow.
? mood:high
- Letter from my twin. Good news. I'll read it out at tea. All four pages.

== near
? act:work
- Let me show you that again. Slowly. There. Once more? Happy to.
? act:leisure
- One tea, one chapter, then bed. Ten sharp. You can set the ship's clock by me.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My twin's on the Halcyon. So are Navarro's and Nakamura's. They find it hilarious.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- The Tevan belt has storms you can hear coming. Rain on a tin roof. I miss the noise.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- My twin's letters come in episodes. I read one a week. Saves the good bits.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening. One tea, one chapter, then bed. You're welcome to the chapter.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh, hello. It's been a while. Sit. Tell me everything. Slowly.

== near
? habit:gardener
- I help in the garden now. Nobody hurries a seed. It's my kind of job.
? place:teacorner
- Tea's a meal if you try. Biscuit, tea, biscuit. Lunch.   #funny

== invite
? tier>=acquaintance
- Tiles in the common room? I'm slow. Very slow. You'll have time to think.
- Film night? I'll stay till ten. Then I'll go to bed. Mid-film. Every time.   #funny

== accept
- Yes, lovely. Not past ten, mind.
- Happy to. Take your time getting there. I'll save a seat.

== decline
- Not tonight. It's nearly ten. You know me. Tomorrow?
? weekday:thu|fri
- Rest day. I'm writing to the Halcyon. Next episode's due. Another time?

== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I read a chapter. I'll tell you the good bit.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I'll tell my twin. They'll tell the Halcyon. You're famous now.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. My twin's letter came early. They timed it. Took them three tries.   #warm

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- That was yours? Nicely done. You took your time. That's how it should be.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- Sit with me before ten? There's something I'd like to say. No rush.

== about
? aff:amadi-asha:friend
- Amadi always finds the best window. I find it second. It's a good system.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Next episode from the Halcyon soon.
- No rush. There's never a rush.
? time:evening
- Ten o'clock soon. Bed. Always.
? act:breakfast
- Skipped breakfast. Tea's a meal.   #funny
? act:work
- Once more, slowly. There.
?

== rumour
- Last time, on the Halcyon...   #funny
- Slowly now. This bit's good.
